 PUT OPTION AGREEMENT


This Put Option Agreement, dated as of June 15 September 29, 2000 (this AAgreement@), is executed by and between Enron Energy Services Operations, Inc., a Delaware corporation (AEESO@) and Danno II, L.L.C. (formerly known as EESO-OC Holdings #1 LLC) Corp., an Oregon corporation (AEnron@) and Danno III, L.L.C., a Delaware limited liability company (AAsset LLC@).

 Recital

Pursuant to an Assignment and Ratification Agreement, dated December 27, 1999 September 29, 2000 and executed by EESO, EESO Enron and Asset LLC, Enron has assigned and transferred to Asset LLC its member interest in Owens Corning Energy LLC, a Delaware limited liability company rights to receive payments under that certain Swap Agreement dated September 22, 2000 between Enron and Enron Energy Services, LLC (the AAsset@).

  Operative Provisions

For good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, EESO Enron and Asset LLC hereby agree as follows:

Section 1. Definitions.   Capitalized terms used and not defined herein shall have the meanings given to those terms in the Facility Agreement.  As used in this Agreement, the following terms have the respective meanings set forth below:

AAsset@ shall have the meaning given to that term in the Recital hereto.

AFacility Agreement@ shall mean that certain Amended and Restated Facility Agreement dated May 31, 2000 and executed by the Trust as issuer of the Notes, Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce, as Agent and the other financial institutions named therein as the same may be amended or supplemented from time to time.

APayment Date@ shall have the same meaning as AApplicable Payment Date@ set forth in the Total Return Swap Agreement.

APrincipal Put Notice@ shall have the meaning given to such term in Section 2 hereof.

APurchase Price@ shall have the meaning set forth in Section 3 hereof.

APut Member Swap Interest@ shall mean an undivided interest in 1% of the Asset.

APut Notice@ means, with respect to any Payment Date, a notice duly executed on behalf of Asset LLC or its assignee in substantially the form of Schedule I hereto, whereby Asset LLC or its assignee requires EESO Enron to purchase the Put Member Swap Interests from Asset LLC on such Payment Date pursuant to the terms of this Put Option Agreement.

Section 2. Purchase of Put Member Swap Interests.  Asset LLC shall have the right but not the obligation to require EESO Enron to repurchase Put Member Swap Interests from Asset LLC on any Payment Date in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.  In the event that Asset LLC elects to require EESO Enron to repurchase Put Member Swap Interests on any Payment Date, Asset LLC shall deliver a Put Notice to EESO Enron not later than seven Business Days prior to such Payment Date, provided that (i) in the event that the obligations of the Trust under the Notes are accelerated under the terms of the Facility Agreement, Asset LLC may deliver a Put Notice at any time on or before the date of such acceleration and (ii) any Put Notice with respect to the Payment Date falling on March 15 29, 2001 shall be delivered on or before January 31 February 14, 2001 (the APrincipal Put Notice@).  Delivery of the Principal Put Notice shall have the effect of signifying that Asset LLC has irrevocably elected to require EESO Enron to repurchase Put Member Swap Interests on each remaining Payment Date beginning March 15 29, 2001.  The number of Put Member Swap Interests specified in each Put Notice may not exceed the number of Put Member Swap Interests which produces an aggregate purchase price equal to the total of all amounts payable by the Trust to the Lenders on the applicable Payment Date.  Any Put Notice delivered by Asset LLC shall be irrevocable.  On any Payment Date with respect to which a Put Notice has been delivered as provided above, Asset LLC shall sell, assign and transfer to EESO Enron the number of Put Member Swap Interests specified in such Put Notice pursuant to an Assignment and Ratification Agreement substantially in the form of Schedule II hereto, and EESO Enron shall pay to Asset LLC the applicable Purchase Price.  Only one Put Notice for each Payment Date may be delivered by Asset LLC hereunder and the aggregate number of Put Member Swap Interests which EESO Enron may be required to purchase hereunder shall not exceed 96.83_____.

Section 3. Purchase Price.  The Purchase Price for the Put Member Swap Interests to be purchased by EESO Enron on any Payment Date in respect of which a Put Notice has been delivered shall be equal to $123,022.34 (one hundred twenty-three thousand twenty-two dollars and thirty-four cents) per Put Member $___________ (_______________________________________________) per Put Swap Interest and shall be paid on the applicable Payment Date in immediately available funds.

Section 4. Warranty.  By delivering a Put Notice, Asset LLC shall be deemed to warrant to EESO Enron that, as of the date of delivery of such Put Notice and as of the relevant Payment Date, Asset LLC holds good title to the Put Member Swap Interests and that there exists no mortgage, pledge, security interest, encumbrance, lien or charge of any kind over such Put Member Swap Interests by, through or under Asset LLC.

Section 5. Notices.  Any notices to be given by either party hereunder may be validly  served in accordance with the procedure set forth in Section 12.02 of the Asset LLC Agreement.

Section 6. Assignment.  EESO Enron acknowledges and agrees that Asset LLC may assign its rights to deliver Put Option Notices under Section 2 hereof to the ultimate owner of in excess of 51% of the economic interest in Asset LLC, which as of the date of this agreement is the Trust.  Following receipt of a written notice from Asset LLC that it has assigned its rights to deliver a Put Notice hereunder, any Put Notice delivered by such assignee shall be binding upon EESO Enron and Asset LLC.


Section 7. Amendment; Third Party Beneficiary.  No amendment or waiver of any provisions of this Put Option Agreement shall be effective unless the same shall be executed in writing by the parties and the Trust.  The Trust is an intended third party beneficiary of this Agreement.

Section 8. Law.  This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the state of Texas.



